  "slug": "check-tally-reports-before-month-end-review",
  "title": "Preparing Tally Reports for a Month-End Review",
  "description": "Use the same reporting period and a small set of reconciliation checks before sharing month-end figures.",
  "category": "Accountant and team workflows",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Set a common review period",
      "body": "Confirm the company, start date and cutoff date with the accounting team. Use the same period in each synced report and in TallyPrime. Write down the last successful sync so the team knows when source corrections could have reached the reports."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spot-check transactions near the cutoff",
      "body": "Choose one voucher near the beginning and one near the end of the period. Match type, number, party and amount with TallyPrime. Check a receipt or credit note if it could explain a difference in a customer's ending balance."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Carry exceptions forward clearly",
      "body": "For any unresolved difference, record the affected report and the voucher or ledger that needs a check. Review source corrections and the subsequent successful sync, then regenerate only the reports that changed and label the new files with their date."
    }
  ],
